# SERVICE

## GoalPhaseService

### DESCRIPTION

Own the selected Phase's entry, assigned semantic/Human completion and mechanical progression. The normal factory publishes startGoalPhase, advanceGoalPhase, submitGoalPhaseWorkResult and submitGoalPhaseOrderedDecision. Session context resolves pending work and native state; callers supply business inputs or requested results, not control envelopes or stages. Configured managed Step/Phase checks, review, closure and repository effects retain their owning authority. Other declarations are not additional normal public stages. Accepted review or a Human answer alone does not establish committed Step, Phase completion or release.

### OPERATION

#### advanceGoalPhase

##### DESCRIPTION

Advance the single execution identified by sessionId. Read native state/pending work directly and absorb managed mechanical progression. Return a typed Request, Human question, Wait or Terminal; work specifies submitOperation, submitSessionId and resultType. Internal RepositorySync work uses its own child session. The caller chooses no stage/Step/transition; only actual whole-Phase/repository completion is Terminal.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseAdvanceInput

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| sessionId | string | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseAdvanceResult

#### submitGoalPhaseWorkResult

##### DESCRIPTION

Consume outcome, summary and findings for the actual pending implementation/repair/review work, plus genuine result/artifact reference and only consumed evidence. Return committed accepted/outcome/message data for chat, not another Request. Submit never calls Advance or claims unexecuted checks, Step/Phase release or remote effects.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseWorkResult

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| sessionId | string | 1 |
| result | GoalPhaseWorkResult | 1 |
| resultReference | WorkflowArtifactReference | 1 |
| completionFacts | WorkflowArtifactReference | * |
| executionEvidence | WorkflowExecutionEvidence | ? |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseWorkSubmissionResult

#### submitGoalPhaseOrderedDecision

##### DESCRIPTION

Consume the pending ordered Human choice/rationale and actual evidence reference. Independent host Human evidence owns consent; authentication or AI output is not consent. ResumeAssignedWork, Defer and Cancel preserve their existing meaning without amending the plan or refunding repairs. Return actual committed acceptance/message; following work requires explicit Advance.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseOrderedDecisionAnswer

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| sessionId | string | 1 |
| answer | GoalPhaseOrderedDecisionAnswer | 1 |
| resultReference | WorkflowArtifactReference | 1 |
| completionFacts | WorkflowArtifactReference | * |
| executionEvidence | WorkflowExecutionEvidence | ? |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseOrderedDecisionSubmissionResult

#### startGoalPhase

##### DESCRIPTION

Start the declared Phase/repository business input. Workflow loads its admitted host business entry directly, assigns a new sessionId when none is proposed and returns that canonical ID with the actual start acknowledgement. A host chat ID is not reused implicitly. Call advanceGoalPhase for next work; Start grants no effect or release authority.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseStartInput

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| input | GoalPhaseStartInput | 1 |
| sessionId | string | ? |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseStartResult

# SERVICE

## SplitPhaseService

### DESCRIPTION

Own SplitPhase entry, assigned semantic/Human completion, deterministic planning and document effects. Session context resolves native instance, planning context and pending work; callers return requested results without duplicated control fields. Workflow owns calibration, packing and progression to Preview or authorized managed Apply. Independent Human evidence and actual document scope remain with their owning host boundaries. Document-conflict handlers are unavailable, not a successful wait or terminal. A completion acknowledgement is not successful application.

### OPERATION

#### startSplitPhase

##### DESCRIPTION

Start sourcePhaseIdentity, invocationMode and optional proposalReference through the admitted host business allocation and actual independent Human/source authority. Allocate and return canonical sessionId when absent, creating this execution's native instance, retained Start and root context. The client does not register/select a context. Start returns an acknowledgement; advanceSplitPhase selects work.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseStartInput

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| input | SplitPhaseStartInput | 1 |
| sessionId | string | ? |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseStartResult

#### submitPartitionSemanticResult

##### DESCRIPTION

Consume the pending partition decision, rationale, requested estimates/boundaries and actual evidence. Workflow owns the result destination, known data, calibration and packing. Enriched/DecisionNeeded is semantic data, not Human consent. Return committed acceptance and useful chat text, not document application or next work; Advance alone progresses.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhasePartitionSemanticResult

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| sessionId | string | 1 |
| result | SplitPhasePartitionSemanticResult | 1 |
| completionFacts | WorkflowArtifactReference | * |
| executionEvidence | WorkflowExecutionEvidence | ? |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseSemanticSubmissionResult

#### advanceSplitPhase

##### DESCRIPTION

Advance sessionId through direct native pending work and owning current business frontier. Absorb deterministic calibration/packing/planning and authorized document effects. Return typed partition/scope/reasoning work, actual scope/reasoning Human question, real Wait or Preview/Apply/stopped Terminal. Work includes submission route/type; no caller stage/candidate/context selector. Unavailable handling is an error.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseAdvanceInput

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| sessionId | string | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseAdvanceResult

#### submitHandoffScopeResult

##### DESCRIPTION

Consume the pending decision, rationale, ordered producing/receiving scopes and evidence. DecisionNeeded contains no partial scopes. Workflow owns assignment/destination. Return actual committed acceptance/message without transferring authority, applying documents or issuing work; call advanceSplitPhase after accepted intake.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseScopeSemanticResult

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| sessionId | string | 1 |
| result | SplitPhaseScopeSemanticResult | 1 |
| completionFacts | WorkflowArtifactReference | * |
| executionEvidence | WorkflowExecutionEvidence | ? |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseScopeSubmissionResult

#### submitReasoningResult

##### DESCRIPTION

Consume the pending decision, rationale, unknown-item assignments and evidence. Workflow owns its destination and objective calculation; the answer supplies no checkpoint or execution grant. Return committed acceptance/message. DecisionNeeded is not Human consent, and intake is not Preview/Apply; explicit Advance chooses following work.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseReasoningSemanticResult

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| sessionId | string | 1 |
| result | SplitPhaseReasoningSemanticResult | 1 |
| completionFacts | WorkflowArtifactReference | * |
| executionEvidence | WorkflowExecutionEvidence | ? |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseReasoningSubmissionResult

#### submitSplitHumanDirection

##### DESCRIPTION

Consume the actual pending scope/reasoning Human choice and evidence reference. ProvideResolution names actual interpretation data; Defer/Cancel has no resolution. The independent host channel attests this question/answer. Return committed acceptance/chat text without eager Advance or document effects. Duplicate/replay/intermediate-recovery guarantees are excluded.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseHumanDirectionAnswer

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| sessionId | string | 1 |
| answer | SplitPhaseHumanDirectionAnswer | 1 |
| resultReference | WorkflowArtifactReference | 1 |
| completionFacts | WorkflowArtifactReference | * |
| executionEvidence | WorkflowExecutionEvidence | ? |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseHumanDirectionSubmissionResult

# SERVICE

## RepositoryHumanService

### DESCRIPTION

Independent Human channel for a retained RepositorySync semantic conflict that
could not be decided. Present the original base/local/remote text and rationale;
do not infer consent from AI output or login identity. Only the exact issued
Decision completion may return the Human answer. This declaration installs no
channel, command executor or source/remote permission.

### OPERATION

#### presentRepositoryConflictDecision

##### DESCRIPTION

Present only the exact Workflow-issued conflict question, including its original
texts and rationale, through the independent Human channel. Return the declared
answer through the assigned completion route; do not substitute an AI judgment
or infer consent from login identity. Workflow verifies the answer and owns later
resolution effects. This operation performs no file, Git or synchronization effect.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncHumanConflictRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncHumanConflictAnswer

# SERVICE

## RepositorySyncService

### DESCRIPTION

Own repository convergence through five normal Operations: Start, advance and assigned conflict/review/Human completion. Session context resolves selected native state and pending work. Workflow owns fetch, preservation, integration, validation, commit, push and final observation through configured fixed managed Git/check capabilities, delegating only requested semantic results or Human answers. Other declarations are not additional normal public stages. Host scope, effect authority and independent evidence remain with their consuming boundaries. A WAIT or accepted review without the actual final repository outcome is not convergence.

### OPERATION

#### startRepositorySync

##### DESCRIPTION

Start the declared repositoryIdentity, localBranch, trackingRemote, trackingBranch, remoteEndpointIdentity and syncMode. Resolve actual host business entry/participant directly, allocate sessionId when absent and return the canonical ID with the start acknowledgement. Start does not fetch/push or grant command/remote authority; owning Advance progresses.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncStartInput

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| input | RepositorySyncStartInput | 1 |
| sessionId | string | ? |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncStartResult

#### advanceRepositorySync

##### DESCRIPTION

Advance the single sessionId execution through direct current state and configured managed Git/check progression. Return typed conflict/review work, actual Human question, real Wait or actual convergence Terminal, with work submission route/type. The caller sends no stage/path/argv/receipt/target selector. Existing scope/effect/evidence owners remain; no replay/intermediate recovery is promised.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncAdvanceInput

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| sessionId | string | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncAdvanceResult

#### submitRepositorySyncWorkResult

##### DESCRIPTION

Consume the pending conflict decision, resolution texts, rationale and genuinely consumed result/evidence reference. The issued work owns coverage and interpretation. Return committed acceptance and useful chat text. A proposal is not write/command/commit/push authority or convergence; only explicit Advance applies authorized following progression.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncConflictResult

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| sessionId | string | 1 |
| result | RepositorySyncConflictResult | 1 |
| resultReference | WorkflowArtifactReference | 1 |
| completionFacts | WorkflowArtifactReference | * |
| executionEvidence | WorkflowExecutionEvidence | ? |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncConflictSubmissionResult

#### submitNativeMergeReview

##### DESCRIPTION

Consume the pending review decision, rationale, findings and actual result/evidence reference. Independent host evidence owns reviewer admission. Return committed acceptance/display text; acceptance alone is not commit/push/convergence and Submit never calls Advance.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncNativeMergeReviewResult

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
